WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.292 --> 00:00:07.042
- Three years ago, I
went skydiving in Dubai.

00:00:09.483 --> 00:00:13.315
Right, skydiving is a really interesting

00:00:13.315 --> 00:00:15.482
confront with fear, right?

00:00:16.509 --> 00:00:17.342
So I got to stand up, so

00:00:17.342 --> 00:00:18.759
I got to stand up.

00:00:20.438 --> 00:00:23.147
So, all your friends,
what happens is you go,

00:00:23.147 --> 00:00:25.157
sorry, I dropped my pen.

00:00:25.157 --> 00:00:28.138
So what happens is you
go out the night before

00:00:28.138 --> 00:00:30.828
and you take a drink with your friends.

00:00:30.828 --> 00:00:34.295
And somebody says, "hey, we
should go skydiving tomorrow!"

00:00:34.295 --> 00:00:38.028
and you go, "Yeah, we'll
go skydiving, yeah!"

00:00:38.028 --> 00:00:40.693
"Yeah" everybody goes, "Yeah!"

00:00:40.693 --> 00:00:44.360
and you go home by
yourself you like, "Umm."

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:50.222
Right, you like, "Well,
they was drunk too."

00:00:50.222 --> 00:00:53.749
"right, so, maybe they not, I mean"

00:00:53.749 --> 00:00:55.056
"we don't have to go."

00:00:55.056 --> 00:00:56.267
"We don't have to do it."

00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:58.436
And then that night
you're laying in your bed

00:00:58.436 --> 00:01:00.822
and you just keep, "Uhh, uhh"

00:01:00.822 --> 00:01:02.112
and you're terrified.

00:01:02.112 --> 00:01:03.936
You keep imagining over and over again

00:01:03.936 --> 00:01:06.097
jumping out of an airplane and you can't

00:01:06.097 --> 00:01:08.353
figure out why you would do that.

00:01:08.353 --> 00:01:10.253
Right, and you're laying there

00:01:10.253 --> 00:01:11.831
and you have the worst night's sleep

00:01:11.831 --> 00:01:12.778
of your life but

00:01:12.778 --> 00:01:14.859
you still have the hope that

00:01:14.859 --> 00:01:16.453
your friends were drunk.

00:01:16.453 --> 00:01:18.439
You wake up the next day and you go

00:01:18.439 --> 00:01:20.522
down where you said you would meet

00:01:20.522 --> 00:01:22.047
and everybody's there.

00:01:22.047 --> 00:01:26.746
And you're like, "Ah, oh,
cool, cool, cool, cool."

00:01:26.746 --> 00:01:29.263
Right, so you get in the van and

00:01:29.263 --> 00:01:31.362
you don't know that your friends had

00:01:31.362 --> 00:01:32.974
the same night that you had,

00:01:32.974 --> 00:01:34.511
cause they're pretending like they didn't.

00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:36.426
They're like, "Yeah, my
uncle's a Navy SEAL,"

00:01:36.426 --> 00:01:38.360
"and hey, you know,
it's going to be great."

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.979
"I've been looking forward to this."

00:01:39.979 --> 00:01:41.733
so you like, "Oh my God, oh my God!"

00:01:41.733 --> 00:01:43.209
and your stomach is terrible,

00:01:43.209 --> 00:01:44.877
you can't eat and everything.

00:01:44.877 --> 00:01:46.678
But you don't want to be the only punk

00:01:46.678 --> 00:01:48.762
who doesn't jump out of this airplane.

00:01:48.762 --> 00:01:52.414
So you get there and then
you have this safety brief.

00:01:52.414 --> 00:01:54.151
And the guys are telling you,

00:01:54.151 --> 00:01:55.635
"Well, if the chute doesn't open"

00:01:55.635 --> 00:01:57.531
"what's going to happen
is you're going to"

00:01:57.531 --> 00:01:59.577
well, what what could happen that

00:01:59.577 --> 00:02:01.723
the chute wouldn't open?

00:02:01.723 --> 00:02:03.855
Right, so you do a thing and what you do

00:02:03.855 --> 00:02:05.781
is your first jump
you're attached to a guy

00:02:05.781 --> 00:02:08.065
who's going to walk you out.

00:02:08.065 --> 00:02:10.241
So you go and you get there

00:02:10.241 --> 00:02:12.979
and there's an airplane
and nobody's stopping,

00:02:12.979 --> 00:02:15.000
everybody's still going.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.882
So you get onto the airplane and

00:02:16.882 --> 00:02:19.001
you're sitting there
and you know it's extra

00:02:19.001 --> 00:02:21.400
because you're sitting on some dude's lap,

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.731
some stranger, you're sitting on his lap.

00:02:23.731 --> 00:02:25.796
And you're trying to make small talk,

00:02:25.796 --> 00:02:26.796
"Yeah, man."

00:02:29.165 --> 00:02:33.332
"So you be jumpin' with
people all the time, huh?"

00:02:34.209 --> 00:02:36.383
So, you know, and then
you got to make sure.

00:02:36.383 --> 00:02:39.979
"You got kids, right, you
got people you need to see."

00:02:39.979 --> 00:02:42.295
Right, you want to make sure he's serious.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.399
And you get in there,
so everything's normal.

00:02:44.399 --> 00:02:46.537
So you fly, you go up and you go up.

00:02:46.537 --> 00:02:48.794
You go up to 14,000 feet and you notice

00:02:48.794 --> 00:02:51.948
there's a light, it's red and it's yellow

00:02:51.948 --> 00:02:53.456
and green, right.

00:02:53.456 --> 00:02:55.381
So, right now the light's red,

00:02:55.381 --> 00:02:57.762
and you think at some point
the light's going to go green.

00:02:57.762 --> 00:03:00.338
And you don't know what's going to happen.

00:03:00.338 --> 00:03:02.579
Right, and you wait and it goes yellow,

00:03:02.579 --> 00:03:04.097
and the light goes green,

00:03:04.097 --> 00:03:05.893
and somebody opens the door.

00:03:05.893 --> 00:03:07.232
And in that moment you realize

00:03:07.232 --> 00:03:08.903
that you've never been
in a friggin' airplane

00:03:08.903 --> 00:03:10.486
with the door open.

00:03:12.287 --> 00:03:15.454
Right, terror, I'm sorry I'm spitting.

00:03:17.557 --> 00:03:21.079
I'm sorry, terror, terror, terror, terror!

00:03:21.079 --> 00:03:23.162
Right, so you go and then

00:03:24.787 --> 00:03:27.717
if you were smart you sat in the back

00:03:27.717 --> 00:03:29.621
so you don't go first.

00:03:29.621 --> 00:03:32.200
Right, and then people start
going out of the airplane.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:35.965
And you go, and the guy walks you up

00:03:35.965 --> 00:03:37.678
to the end of the thing.

00:03:37.678 --> 00:03:40.974
And you're standing at
your toes are on the edge,

00:03:40.974 --> 00:03:44.057
and you're looking out down to death.

00:03:46.821 --> 00:03:49.153
And they say, "On three!"

00:03:49.153 --> 00:03:51.011
And they say, "One, two!"

00:03:51.011 --> 00:03:53.072
and he pushes you on two because

00:03:53.072 --> 00:03:55.405
people grab on three, right.

00:03:56.453 --> 00:03:58.834
- (laughing)

00:03:58.834 --> 00:04:01.837
- Right, and you go, "Uhhhh!"

00:04:01.837 --> 00:04:06.054
you fall out of the
airplane and in one second

00:04:06.054 --> 00:04:10.782
you realize that it's the
most blissful experience

00:04:10.782 --> 00:04:13.115
of your life, you're flying.

00:04:14.173 --> 00:04:16.967
Right, it doesn't feel
like falling, right.

00:04:16.967 --> 00:04:19.583
You're actually kind of held a little bit

00:04:19.583 --> 00:04:21.603
by the wind and then you start,

00:04:21.603 --> 00:04:23.594
you start falling, you're falling,

00:04:23.594 --> 00:04:25.751
and there's zero fear.

00:04:25.751 --> 00:04:29.213
You realize at the point of maximum danger

00:04:29.213 --> 00:04:32.327
is the point of minimum fear.

00:04:32.327 --> 00:04:33.244
It's bliss!

00:04:34.259 --> 00:04:35.176
It's bliss!

00:04:36.034 --> 00:04:38.117
And you're flying, right,

00:04:39.439 --> 00:04:41.891
and you're doing it and then

00:04:41.891 --> 00:04:45.071
20 seconds, 25 seconds, 40 seconds,

00:04:45.071 --> 00:04:47.673
and you have enough time to like,

00:04:47.673 --> 00:04:51.409
"There's that building, that's how I like"

00:04:51.409 --> 00:04:53.517
"Oh, you can see the ocean!"

00:04:53.517 --> 00:04:56.479
Right, you start doing all of that,

00:04:56.479 --> 00:04:59.227
and the lesson for me
is why were you scared

00:04:59.227 --> 00:05:01.666
in your bed the night before?

00:05:01.666 --> 00:05:04.137
What do you need that fear for?

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:05.553
Just don't go!

00:05:05.553 --> 00:05:10.075
Why are you scared in your
bed 16 hours before you jump?

00:05:10.075 --> 00:05:12.349
Why are you scared in the car?

00:05:12.349 --> 00:05:15.069
Why could you not enjoy breakfast?

00:05:15.069 --> 00:05:17.319
What did you need, fear is,

00:05:18.888 --> 00:05:19.971
fear of what?

00:05:20.828 --> 00:05:23.055
You're nowhere even near the airplane.

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:26.150
Everything up to the stepping out,

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:28.944
there's actually no reason to be scared.

00:05:28.944 --> 00:05:31.689
It only just ruins your day.

00:05:31.689 --> 00:05:33.614
You don't have to jump.

00:05:33.614 --> 00:05:35.193
And then in that moment,

00:05:35.193 --> 00:05:37.715
all of sudden when you
should be terrified,

00:05:37.715 --> 00:05:41.094
is the most blissful
experience of your life.

00:05:41.094 --> 00:05:44.639
And God placed the best things in life

00:05:44.639 --> 00:05:47.445
on the other side of terror.

00:05:47.445 --> 00:05:49.591
On the other side of your maximum fear

00:05:49.591 --> 00:05:52.427
are all of the best things in life.

00:05:52.427 --> 00:05:54.774
You know, so that was sorry.

00:05:54.774 --> 00:05:58.965
Sorry, that was my experience
with skydiving and fear.

00:05:58.965 --> 00:06:01.799
- So practically speaking.

00:06:01.799 --> 00:06:03.384
- But I didn't like that take,

00:06:03.384 --> 00:06:05.576
I'm going to do it again.

00:06:05.576 --> 00:06:06.946
I can sell it better.

00:06:06.946 --> 00:06:08.863
I can sell that better.

00:06:09.794 --> 00:06:13.294
The confrontation with fear is an absolute

00:06:14.291 --> 00:06:16.562
magical way of facing the things we have

00:06:16.562 --> 00:06:18.326
to do in this life, you know.

00:06:18.326 --> 00:06:21.409
Forget security, live for experience.

